  data: {
    LLM: 'Do not play for money in street settings—it is a scam; the dealer uses sleight of hand and accomplices (shills) so the punter cannot win.\n\nIf playing honestly with friends with no real money, the only skill is visual tracking of the queen during the mix; the dealer can make this very difficult.\n\nSources advise: play only with no real money involved and explain the trick afterwards. In a true monte scam the mark has no chance of winning.',
